# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
#  Dockerfile.blackwell-vllm
#  Extends nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.03-py3 with Gemma 4 support.
#
#  Strategy: surgical patch — copies only the Gemma 4 Python files
#  from upstream vllm 0.19.0 into the NVIDIA 0.17.1 installation,
#  preserving all Blackwell-specific compiled kernels (FlashInfer
#  SM_121, custom Triton, Flash Attention, CUTLASS).
#
#  Build:
#    docker build -f ray-cluster/Dockerfile.blackwell-vllm -t blackwell-vllm:latest ray-cluster/
#    # or: just build-blackwell
#
#  Run (Ray head node):
#    docker run --gpus all --network host \
#      -v ~/.cache/huggingface:/root/.cache/huggingface \
#      blackwell-vllm:latest
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

FROM nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.03-py3

ENV VLLM=/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/vllm

# ── 1. Upgrade transformers (adds gemma4 to CONFIG_MAPPING_NAMES) ──────────
RUN pip install "transformers>=5.0" --quiet 2>&1 | grep -E "Successfully|already|ERROR" || true

# ── 2. Download vllm 0.19.0 wheel and extract Gemma 4 source files ─────────
RUN pip download vllm==0.19.0 --no-deps -d /tmp/vllm_dl --quiet 2>/dev/null \
 && mkdir -p /tmp/vllm_src \
 && cd /tmp/vllm_src \
 && unzip -q /tmp/vllm_dl/vllm-0.19.0-*.whl

# ── 3. Copy Gemma 4 Python implementation files ────────────────────────────
RUN cp /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4.py \
       /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py \
       /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_utils.py \
       ${VLLM}/model_executor/models/ \
 && cp /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/model_executor/layers/rotary_embedding/gemma4_rope.py \
       ${VLLM}/model_executor/layers/rotary_embedding/ \
 && cp /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_utils.py \
       /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/tool_parsers/gemma4_tool_parser.py \
       ${VLLM}/tool_parsers/ \
 && cp /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/reasoning/gemma4_utils.py \
       /tmp/vllm_src/vllm/reasoning/gemma4_reasoning_parser.py \
       ${VLLM}/reasoning/

# ── 4-8. Patch all registries with a single Python script ─────────────────
COPY patch_gemma4.py /tmp/patch_gemma4.py
RUN python3 /tmp/patch_gemma4.py

# ── 9. Verify Gemma 4 is fully registered ─────────────────────────────────
RUN python3 -c "\
from vllm.model_executor.models.registry import ModelRegistry; \
archs = ModelRegistry.get_supported_archs(); \
gemma4 = [a for a in archs if 'Gemma4' in a]; \
assert gemma4, 'Gemma4 NOT registered!'; \
print('Gemma4 registered:', gemma4); \
from vllm.model_executor.layers.rotary_embedding import Gemma4RotaryEmbedding; \
print('Gemma4RotaryEmbedding: OK'); \
from transformers.models.auto.configuration_auto import CONFIG_MAPPING_NAMES; \
assert 'gemma4' in CONFIG_MAPPING_NAMES, 'gemma4 not in transformers!'; \
print('transformers gemma4: OK'); \
"

# ── 10. Cleanup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
RUN rm -rf /tmp/vllm_src /tmp/vllm_dl /tmp/patch_gemma4.py

# ── Ray head node entrypoint ───────────────────────────────────────────────
ENV RAY_HEAD_IP=192.168.200.12

ENTRYPOINT ["/bin/bash", "-c"]
CMD ["ray start --block --head --node-ip-address=${RAY_HEAD_IP} --port=6379"]
